  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Roupp gave them six scoreless innings. That's how they won this one.",
    "what_this_means": "Landen Roupp shut down St. Louis over six innings with just two hits allowed. Christian Koss and Bryce Eldridge each hit solo homers. That was the Giants' entire offense, six hits and nothing else. They never trailed, led from the first inning through the final out, and held on by a single run. Joel Kuhnel closed it with 1.1 innings of work, giving up one run but keeping the game intact. This is not a dominant performance. This is precision under control, which right now is what this team needs to look like. They won by one run for the second straight night. That margin keeps getting smaller.",
    "what_to_watch": "Andre Pallante takes the mound tonight for St. Louis with a 3.51 ERA. This is a pitcher who has looked sharp. Blade Tidwell goes for the Giants in a midday game that could set the tone for the series stretch run. One run wins twice in two days. That does not scale.",
